      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/test-engineer.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A test never reads `test/results/` as a fixture",
      "prov:value": "Derived QA results are leaving `main` for the orphan `qa-reports` branch\n(arc `3fva`): the checkout's `<instance>/test/results/**` is a working copy,\nstill committed until bean `5hox` removes it, and the record is the\ncommit-keyed entry `qa-publish` stores.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5hox",
        "bean 3fva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/test-engineer.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "A test never reads `test/results/` as a fixture",
      "prov:value": "A test that reads that tree is\nreading a file that will not be there — and the readers audit\n(`docs/proposals/qa-readers-audit-2026-10-01.md` §5.5) measured what that\ncosts: 15 tests in 6 files fail only when the corpus is absent, and one,\n*\"no critical criterion is failing\"*, **passes** when it is absent because it\niterates over zero files.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-01",
        "docs/proposals/qa-readers-audit-2026-10-01.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/test-engineer.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every test has a Gherkin (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner ruling: \"A test should always have a Gherkin.\" Made a harness rule with a QA flag under work item cat-harness-724x.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-06",
        "cat-harness-724x"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/test-engineer.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every test has a Gherkin (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner decision: binding is by tag (no execution engine required); a Scenario may also bind a WHO-ITB GITB TDL test case with @itb:<testSuite id>/<testCase id>, the tag schemes are an extensible list, and Gherkin dialects are allowed so translated .feature files remain valid. Relayed by the session working the ITB side.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-07",
        "cat-harness-724x"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-07"
      ]
